## Why This Is Asked

Probes production-grade multi-tenant routing with cost control, latency targets, RBAC, and integration with Azure services (Cosmos DB, AD, Cognitive Search, Durable Functions, API Management). Assesses ability to design end-to-end data flow, observability, and testing strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant policy and quota management in Cosmos DB
- Multi-model routing: cost-aware model choice + RAG grounding
- Latency budgets and backpressure via Durable Functions
- RBAC via Azure AD and API Management gating
- Grounding via Cognitive Search KB

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal routing decision
function chooseEngine(policies, tenantId, workload) {
  const p = policies[tenantId];
  if (!p) return 'GPT-3.5-turbo';
  if (workload.latencyMs > p.latencyBudget) return p.defaultModel;
  if (workload.costPerRequest > p.costBudget) return 'GPT-3.5-turbo';
  return p.preferredModel;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you model tenant quotas in Cosmos DB for fairness during bursts?
- What tests validate SLA adherence under canary deployments?
- How would you implement backpressure across regional deployments and API gateways?

## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to translate regulatory requirements into automated, auditable technical controls using Azure AI and governance services, with strict multi-tenant isolation requirements.

## Key Concepts

- Regulatory-to-controls mapping (GDPR/CCPA/NIST)
- Knowledge base grounding with Cognitive Search
- Per-tenant RBAC and data isolation
- Automated evidence collection and auditable logging
- Azure Policy integration for continuous enforcement

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: Map obligations to controls and enforce per-tenant policy
async function ensureCompliance(clientId) {
  const obligations = await kb.fetchObligations(clientId);
  const controls = await mapToControls(obligations);

  const evidence = await collectEvidence(clientId, controls);
  const violations = await evaluateAgainstPolicy(controls, evidence);

  await logDecision({ clientId, obligations, controls, evidence, violations });
  return generateRemediationPlan(violations);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

